,"line":17},{"title":"an entire website","target":"http://callbackhell.com/","line":25},{"title":"“What Color is Your Function?”","target":"https://journal.stuffwithstuff.com/2015/02/01/what-color-is-your-function/","line":99},{"title":"“The C10K Problem.”","target":"http://www.kegel.com/c10k.html","line":180},{"title":"“What Color is Your Function?”","target":"https://journal.stuffwithstuff.com/2015/02/01/what-color-is-your-function/","line":181},{"title":"“How Do You Color Your Functions?”","target":"https://elizarov.medium.com/how-do-you-color-your-functions-a6bb423d936d","line":182},{"title":"“Zig’s New Async I/O.”","target":"https://kristoff.it/blog/zig-new-async-io/","line":183},{"title":"“Virtual Threads in Java.”","target":"https://blogs.oracle.com/javamagazine/java-virtual-threads/","line":184},{"title":"“The State of Async Rust: Runtimes.”","target":"https://corrode.dev/blog/async/","line":185},{"title":"“Never Snooze a Future.”","target":"https://jacko.io/snooze.html","line":186}],"metadata":{"title":"What Async Promised and What it Delivered","source":"https://causality.blog/essays/what-async-promised/","author":null,"published":null,"created":"2026-04-26","description":"The async/await saga is a story where each chapter solves the previous chapter's worst problem while introducing new structural costs. The sequential syntax that made async code readable also obscures the thing that matters: which operations actually depend on each other.","tags":["#clippings"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[43,58],[76,91],[121,128],[134,143]],"key":"resrc/clippings/What Async Promised and What it Delivered.md"},
